# AI Assistant Architecture Reference

When working on the AI chatbot, routing, generation, or API client code, read `docs/AI_ASSISTANT_ARCHITECTURE.md` for the full end-to-end flow:

- Two primary paths: "This Slide" (fast single-slide) vs "Deck" (router + plan + execution)
- Router pipeline: AI router (LLM-based) with rule-based fallback
- Generation functions: `generateSlides()`, `fillTemplateWithAI()`, `improveSlide()`
- API layer: `callWithModelFallback()` -> `callGeminiAPI()` (handles all providers)
- Model resolution: `getCredentials()` maps `providerId:modelName` to API config
- Web search: two integration points (router-level and This Slide-level)
- Inactive features: Agent mode, Report mode, Vibe system, Image mode

Reference created 2026-03-31.
